      "synopsis": "Impact investing seeks to generate both financial returns and measurable social or environmental impact. This course offers an applied, case-based exploration of international impact investing, moving from the historical foundations of global CSR practices to the detailed processes of impact vetting, due diligence, and financing mechanisms such as impact bonds and green/blue bonds. Students will engage deeply with real-world dilemmas faced by international investors, analyzing investment opportunities across diverse national contexts.",
      "synopsisHeading": "SYNOPSIS / OVERVIEW",
      "synopsisPage": 20,
      "learningOutcomes": "1. Understand the international evolution from CSR to impact investing and distinguish impact investing from related concepts (ESG, philanthropy, traditional finance).\n2. Apply frameworks for vetting and conducting due diligence on international impact investment opportunities.\n3. Analyze and evaluate impact bonds (DIBs, SIBs) and green/social/sustainability/blue bonds in an international context. Page 1 of 4 Pré-expérience / Pre-experience 2026-2027",
      "learningOutcomesHeading": "OBJECTIFS PEDAGOGIQUES / LEARNING OUTCOMES",
