      "synopsis": "This course is designed for participants who show:\n• a curiosity to learn and understand the luxury business model\n• an interest for different ways of doing business\n• a taste for refined goods and services It introduces them to key concepts and principles of luxury management. The curriculum starts out with an indepth understanding of luxury, its role in society and the key principles defining it. There is a particular focus on luxury brand management as well as the strategic perspectives and challenges for luxury brands in today’s world. To end this course, and to implement its key learnings, students will hand-in a final paper providing their vision for a luxury brand of their choice. Understanding the soul of these iconic brands is key to manage them well. I met many successful executives and what they all have in common, beyond their exceptional skills, is their passion and a deeply anchored understanding of the intangibles of these luxury brands. This course does not pretend to be a fully comprehensive luxury management course. Instead, it provides one approach, mostly based on French luxury brands examples, which differ from the Italian or American or Asian vision. It aims at inspiring you to develop your own vision and your own style. Hopefully, this is what this course will encourage you to do with a variety of teaching tools.",
      "synopsisHeading": "SYNOPSIS",
      "synopsisPage": 27,
      "pedagogicalObjectives": "• Achieve familiarity with the luxury sector, its products and services.\n• Understand the key specificities of the luxury business in terms of managerial practices.\n• Apply the key management principles in the luxury industry to make appropriate business decisions.\n• Describe and analyze the characteristics of a luxury brand and get a sense of the prerequisites to be able to build one over time.\n• Develop and formulate a luxury strategy based on the offering’s characteristics and market opportunities. Skills: Participants will have developed a robust skill set that empowers them to navigate the luxury industry in a global context.\n1. Luxury Brand Analysis: Ability to identify and articulate key characteristics of luxury products and brands, and analyze their market differentiation from premium goods.\n2. Consumer Insight and Behavior: Skills in categorizing luxury consumption motivations and understanding crosscultural perceptions to enhance brand strategy and consumer engagement. Page 3 of 5 Pre-experience ACADEMIC YEAR 2026-27\n3. Strategic Brand Management: Proficiency in developing and managing luxury brand strategies, including brand positioning, pricing tiers, and evaluating brand extensions.\n4. Customer Journey Mapping: Ability to design and optimize customer journeys across multiple touchpoints, ensuring meaningful and immersive brand experiences.\n5. Creative and Business Integration: Skills to balance creative aspirations with business objectives. Course organization - detailed outline: (Number of sessions with their duration and content in order) Session 1 Monday 22/02/2027 09H40-12H50 Rimowa case Session 2 Monday 22/02/2027 14H40-17H50 Mao Geping case Session 3 Wednesday 24/02/2027 08H00-11H10 Session 4 Thursday 25/02/2027 13H00-16H10 Mathieu case Session 5 Monday 08/03/2027 14H40-17H50 Session 6 Thursday 11/03/2027 13H00-16H10 Final Project TEACHING MATERIALS See online content.",
      "pedagogicalObjectivesHeading": "Pedagogical Objectives",
      "totalSessions": 12,
      "totalHours": 18.0
