      "synopsis": "This syllabus is designed for today’s rapidly evolving global environment. It draws on several leading international trend reports. Together, these sources provide a comprehensive view of the forces reshaping economies, industries, governments, and societies worldwide. These reports highlight a world increasingly shaped by advances in artificial intelligence and digital technologies, the climate and energy transition, geoeconomic fragmentation, demographic shifts, workforce transformation, and growing institutional uncertainty. Organizations across sectors are being challenged to rethink their strategies, business models, leadership approaches, and capabilities in response to these interconnected developments. The course examines today's major megatrends and explores their implications for business, public policy, and society. Particular emphasis is placed on the climate and energy transition, as well as technological and AIdriven transformation, while also considering the broader economic, social, and geopolitical forces that influence decision-making and supply chains in an increasingly complex and uncertain world. Through cases, discussions, and scenario-based analysis, participants will develop the ability to understand emerging trends, assess their potential impact, and identify strategic opportunities and risks.",
      "synopsisHeading": "SYNOPSIS / OVERVIEW",
      "synopsisPage": 32,
      "learningOutcomes": "By the end of this course, participants will be able to:\n1. Explain the major global mega trends shaping business, society, government, and daily life.\n2. Distinguish between short-term hype, structural change, and long-term transformation.\n3. Analyze the opportunities, risks, and ethical dilemmas created by each mega trend.\n4. Use basic foresight tools such as trend mapping, scenario building, and strategic implications analysis.\n5. Develop a practical response plan for an organization, community, or sector affected by mega trends. Page 1 of 7 Pré-expérience / Pre-experience 2026-2027",
      "learningOutcomesHeading": "OBJECTIFS PEDAGOGIQUES / LEARNING OUTCOMES",
      "totalSessions": 12,
