      "synopsis": "Most graduates of HEC Paris begin their careers in the professional and financial services (PSF) sectors: consulting, investment banking, business advisory, etc. While all students know the names of the largest firms, and some will have some professional experience inside these firms, most students do not understand how they function and why an understanding of the challenges leaders face can accelerate their career. How is value created? What are the kinds of strategic decisions leaders make and how are they interconnected? Do they even need to have a strategy? If you want to advance in these kinds of organizations, having the answers to such questions will set you apart from the rest. Professional and financial services firms are unlike any other businesses. Their competitive advantage resides in the quality of their people, their interactions, the depth of client relationships, and the ability to turn individual expertise into collective performance. Understanding these dynamics allows you to see why some firms grow while others stall, why the best individual performers don't always become the best leaders, and why client relationships are strategic assets, not sales targets. The course has two distinct elements: (i) concept introduction and (ii) application. Working in groups, each session first explores a distinct strategic challenge through a specially designed case, before groups assume the role of a management team where they apply what they have learned by making management decisions in a multi-session strategic simulation built around a single advisory firm. You formulate your decisions using whatever AI / software tool you deem appropriate according to the scenario, and the data you are provided with. Your management decisions build across sessions, culminating in a Board Decision Memo presented to the other “voting partners” in the classroom which tests whether you have built a strategy that coheres and is defensible.",
      "synopsisHeading": "OVERVIEW",
      "synopsisPage": 42,
      "learningOutcomes": "By the end of this course, you will be able to:\n- Explain how professional and financial services firms function: the economics, internal structures, and strategic elements that separate successful firms from unsuccessful ones. © John Mawdsley 2026. All rights reserved\n- Evaluate the internal and external strategic challenges that these firms face in the same way, or better, than effective leaders do, and construct well-reasoned responses to them.\n- Understand what it means to work inside one of these firms: how professionals are developed, how careers progress, and what really drives profit and performance.\n- Make strategic decisions, defend them under pressure, and understand how early choices affect future strategic options.\n- Develop a clearer view of which firms and roles fit your strengths, and what it takes to build a sustainable career once you join.",
      "learningOutcomesHeading": "LEARNING OUTCOMES",
      "totalSessions": 12,
      "totalHours": 18.0
